error[L0346]: a variant is a name or a list that starts with a name
 --> expand/defenum_errors.knv:1:26
  |
1 | (defenum unnamed-variant 3)
  |                          ^ here
  |
  = help: write it as `name`, `(name type ...)` or `(name :field type ...)`

error[L0346]: a variant is a name or a list that starts with a name
 --> expand/defenum_errors.knv:3:26
  |
3 | (defenum keyword-variant :circle)
  |                          ^^^^^^^ here
  |
  = help: write it as `name`, `(name type ...)` or `(name :field type ...)`

error[L0347]: a variant writes its fields flat
 --> expand/defenum_errors.knv:6:12
  |
6 |   (labeled (struct (text string))))
  |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ here
  |
  = help: write them after its name, as in (labeled :text string :size f64)

error[L0348]: this variant's first item is a type, so it takes no fields
 --> expand/defenum_errors.knv:8:43
  |
8 | (defenum field-after-type (labeled string :size f64))
  |                                           ^^^^^ here
  |
  = help: write only types, or give every item a `:field`

error[L0348]: a field must start with `:`
  --> expand/defenum_errors.knv:10:49
   |
10 | (defenum type-after-field (labeled :text string f64))
   |                                                 ^^^ here
   |
   = help: write each field as `:name type`, as in (labeled :text string)

error[L0349]: this field has no type
  --> expand/defenum_errors.knv:12:38
   |
12 | (defenum field-without-type (labeled :text :size f64))
   |                                      ^^^^^ here
   |
   = help: write a type after it, as in :text i64

error[L0349]: this field has no type
  --> expand/defenum_errors.knv:14:43
   |
14 | (defenum last-field-without-type (labeled :text))
   |                                           ^^^^^ here
   |
   = help: write a type after it, as in :text i64

error[L0340]: the `rust` clause comes right after the name
  --> expand/defenum_errors.knv:18:3
   |
18 |   (rust "Path"))
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ here
   |
   = help: move it to the first place after the name, or after the docstring

error[L0341]: a `rust` clause on `defenum` holds one string, then an optional `bare`
  --> expand/defenum_errors.knv:25:3
   |
25 |   (rust "Holder" "Other")
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ here
   |
   = help: write it as `(rust "Path")` or `(rust "Path" bare)`

error[L0341]: a `rust` clause on `defenum` holds one string, then an optional `bare`
  --> expand/defenum_errors.knv:29:3
   |
29 |   (rust "Holder" plain)
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ here
   |
   = help: write it as `(rust "Path")` or `(rust "Path" bare)`

error[L0339]: `defenum` needs a name
  --> expand/defenum_errors.knv:32:10
